<title>DENMARK: Denmark's Unidanmark climbs on fee hike.</title>
<headline>Denmark's Unidanmark climbs on fee hike.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish banking group Unidanmark's share rose by 8.7 crowns -- 2.76 percent -- on the Copenhagen stock exchange on Monday after announcing a rise in customer service charges at its core Unibank.</p>
<p>At 1200 GMT the share traded at 320 crowns, compared to Friday's closing 311.3, after earlier touching an all-time intra-day high of 323 crowns.</p>
<p>The bank said it was raising fees for cheques, counter withdrawals, giro payments and telephone transfers for private and business customers.</p>
<p>--Steve Weizman, Copenhagen newsroom +45 33969650</p>
</text>
